<p class="c22 title" id="h.susqyrxaksen"><span class="c11 c23">Confidentiality Policy</span></p><p class="c8 c14 c21 subtitle" id="h.5r4msms3s1"><span class="c16 c3">Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0 (RIIS 2.0)</span></p><p class="c10 subtitle" id="h.bizw64ekjq5l"><span class="c3 c16">California Nonprofit Public Benefit Corporation (Incorporated 2025)</span></p><p class="c8"><span class="c5 c3">Approval Date: 2025-09-30 &bull; Effective Date: 2025-09-30 &bull; Version: 1.0 </span></p><p class="c8"><span class="c5 c3">Approved by: Interim Council 2025-09-30</span></p><h1 class="c7" id="h.4kb5ajfhne2i"><span class="c1">1. Purpose</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">The purpose of this policy is to protect the confidentiality of sensitive information shared within the Council and Working Groups of RIIS 2.0. Maintaining confidentiality ensures trust, compliance with legal and fiduciary obligations, and the effective governance of the Institute.</span></p><h1 class="c12" id="h.47yajzqwcie8"><span class="c1">2. Scope</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">This policy applies to:</span></p><ul class="c9 lst-kix_6bibotddhxrl-0 start"><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">All members of the Council (Interim or Elected).</span></li><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">All members of the Working Groups established by the Council.</span></li><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Any other individuals granted access to Council or Working Group deliberations or records.</span></li></ul><h1 class="c7" id="h.auqgeiodfl6i"><span class="c1">3. Definition of Confidential Information</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">Confidential information includes, but is not limited to:</span></p><ul class="c9 lst-kix_a62gpwp9p94o-0 start"><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Draft policies, internal reports, or documents not yet approved for public release.</span></li><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Financial information, donor records, and membership data.</span></li><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Legal advice, contracts, and matters under the attorney&ndash;client privilege.</span></li><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Personal or sensitive information about Fellows, Associates, staff, or volunteers.</span></li><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Deliberations of the Council and Working Groups, including votes and internal discussions, except where explicitly authorized for public dissemination.</span></li><li class="c2 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Sensitive security information related to core </span><span class="c3">technical</span><span class="c5 c3">&nbsp;infrastructure, passwords, access keys, etc.</span></li></ul><h1 class="c7" id="h.2ob495bsb1jx"><span class="c1">4. Obligations</span></h1><p class="c0 c18"><span class="c3">4.1 </span><span class="c15">Duty of Care</span><span class="c3 c5">: Members must treat confidential information with the highest degree of care and discretion.</span></p><p class="c0 c18"><span class="c3">4.2 </span><span class="c15">Use Restrictions</span><span class="c5 c3">: Confidential information shall only be used for purposes directly related to RIIS 2.0 governance, operations, or scholarly mission.</span></p><p class="c0 c18"><span class="c3">4.3 </span><span class="c15">Non-Disclosure</span><span class="c5 c3">: Members may not disclose confidential information to unauthorized persons, including other Affiliates or the public, unless specifically authorized by the Council.</span></p><p class="c0 c18"><span class="c3">4.4 </span><span class="c15">Records Handling</span><span class="c5 c3">: All confidential records must be stored securely. Members shall comply with RIIS 2.0&rsquo;s Privacy Policy, Document Retention Policy, and applicable law in handling such records.</span></p><p class="c0 c18"><span class="c3">4.5 </span><span class="c15">Council Transparency Exception</span><span class="c5 c3">: Consistent with RIIS 2.0&rsquo;s values of transparency, summaries of Council decisions approved for release may be shared with the Fellows, provided such disclosures do not reveal confidential or sensitive material.</span></p><h1 class="c7" id="h.q0nmteyoc1on"><span class="c1">5. Exceptions</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">Confidential information may be disclosed only when:</span></p><ul class="c9 lst-kix_17lnq1x5qzzv-0 start"><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Required by law, regulation, or court order.</span></li><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Authorized in writing by the Council.</span></li><li class="c4 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Necessary to carry out fiduciary duties, provided appropriate safeguards are observed.</span></li></ul><h1 class="c7" id="h.lh6yjf1uvoh2"><span class="c1">6. Duration of Obligation</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">The duty of confidentiality continues indefinitely, even after a member&rsquo;s service on the Council or a Working Group has ended.</span></p><h1 class="c7" id="h.l3v3xtgv7vy6"><span class="c1">7. Violations</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">Breaches of this policy may result in corrective action, including but not limited to removal from a Working Group, removal from the Council (in accordance with Bylaws), or termination of membership in RIIS 2.0, subject to the Conflict Resolution Policy.</span></p><h1 class="c7" id="h.z53gdesbb8pm"><span>8. Acknowledgment</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">All Council members and Working Group members shall annually sign or electronically acknowledge this policy, affirming that they:</span></p><ul class="c9 lst-kix_g916b03uor37-0 start"><li class="c0 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Have received a copy of the policy.</span></li><li class="c0 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Have read and understood the policy.</span></li><li class="c0 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Agree to comply with the policy.</span></li></ul><h1 class="c7" id="h.ojhyr1d6t8in"><span class="c1">9. Review and Amendments</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">This policy shall be reviewed at least every three years or sooner if required by law, organizational needs, or upon recommendation by the Council.</span></p><h1 class="c7 c14" id="h.1lb0ihyqu3qs"><span class="c1">10. Document History:</span></h1><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">Document created by Rami Saydjari 2025-09-18</span></p><p class="c0"><span class="c15">Council Approval: 2025-09-30<br></span><span class="c5 c3">Signed: </span><span style="overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; margin: 0.00px 0.00px; border: 0.00px solid #000000; transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); width: 261.62px; height: 106.85px;"><img alt="" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdUYP5ActXRKG9OfHjkG45IWbLW-RfzHBf2uoV5NZYRzs3tfodR_yINOKDUJJlA8BcTjenyZGzJ4l2Px2cPaRH0jBI6Th2VKycAiPwoUgR6W3o1E8zvQhYuUZa0PP3Ld4eQBpjd2whIqMkVEE2zSrek?key=rEw0AraA2CyjAehjfzZrow" style="width: 261.62px; height: 106.85px; margin-left: 0.00px; margin-top: 0.00px; transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px);" title=""></span></p><p class="c0 c6 c18 c19"><span class="c5 c3"></span></p><p class="c0 c6"><span class="c5 c3"></span></p><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">___________________________<br>Rami Saydjari</span></p><p class="c0"><span class="c5 c3">Secretary of RIIS 2.0</span></p><p class="c0 c6"><span class="c5 c3"></span></p><div><p class="c6 c17"><span class="c5 c11"></span></p></div></body></html>